# Truncate the 30.9 GB Error Log and Bound Its Growth

## Step

`/Users/Shared/joelclaw/logs/inngest/launchd.err.log` is 30.9 GB of lease-failure spam. Sample what matters (error-type census, first/last timestamps) into an asset, then truncate in place (`sudo truncate -s 0`, keeps launchd's inode — no restart; skip the 30 GB incident copy unless disk headroom is proven), and install a `newsyslog.d` rule bounding both Inngest launchd logs. HITL because every command here is sudo (gated per the brief's Notes): produce the exact commands and run them with Joel present or hand them to him. Resolved when the log is under 10 MB and a rotation rule exists.

## Result (2026-07-24 — closed, install remains HITL)

Census captured first ([asset](./asset-inngest-errlog-census.svx)): 35.3 GB spanning since June 17, >99% paired lease-spam lines, plus a June-era `rejecting event; event key not recognized` population worth a someday-look. Joel ran the original truncate on 2026-07-20; the file later regrew to 3.5 GB. The fixed zero-EnvID storm was no longer the steady-state driver: INFO logs grew at about 187 MB/day.

`newsyslog` was rejected with an isolated launchd proof. Forced rotation created a new live inode, while launchd's writer kept appending to the renamed `.0` file. Plain copy-then-truncate was also rejected because writes between copy and truncate can disappear.

Built `infra/central/native/rotate-service-logs.sh` plus a system LaunchDaemon, installer, offline drill, and [operator notes](../../../infra/central/native/LOG_ROTATION.md). The rotator runs as `joelclaw:staff`, checks every 60 seconds, rotates at 64 MiB or 24 hours, and retains seven archives plus the live file. It covers both Inngest launchd logs and the same-class 116 MB Typesense application log. The retained ceiling is about 1.5 GiB across those three logs, plus one check interval of growth.

Rotation stops the one expected writer, takes an APFS copy-on-write snapshot, truncates the same live inode, and resumes the writer before reducing the snapshot to its newest 64 MiB. Every pause is recorded in state and the unified log. The final full-64-MiB offline drill measured an 80 ms pause; an earlier repeat measured 66 ms. A 500 ms group budget fails closed before truncation. Inngest v1.28.0's shortest relevant partition lease is 4 seconds; queue-item leases are 30 seconds and renew every 15 seconds.

The drill proved inode and PID survival, contiguous sequence numbers across rotation, post-rotation writes, size and age triggers, seven-archive retention, full 64 MiB handling, the pause guard, and non-zero failure propagation. `sh -n`, `plutil -lint`, and `git diff --check` passed.

Joel decided on 2026-07-24 to keep `--log-level info` while staleness alarms and registration/run assertions are hardened. The standing recommendation is to revisit `warn` after those alarms are proven; the installer does not change the Inngest wrapper.

Nothing was installed, restarted, committed, or applied to live logs. Exact HITL install command:

```bash
cd /Users/joel/Code/joelhooks/joelclaw
sudo infra/central/native/install-log-rotation.sh --acknowledge-first-rotation
```
